Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 09:20:33 2026 +1000

    Disable ovs_create_tap for ML2/OVS deployments.
    
    Neutron's ML2/OVS mechanism driver gained an `ovs_create_tap` flag in
    a818987db ("ml2: Add ``ovs_create_tap`` flag to ML2/OVS mechanism
    driver", 2026-07-31), mirroring the existing ML2/OVN support. It
    defaults to True and is set in vif_details for any kernel datapath
    port that is not VNIC_DIRECT -- notably without consulting
    OVS_HYBRID_PLUG.
    
    Kolla-Ansible hardcodes the OVS hybrid iptables firewall driver in
    the openvswitch agent config, so hybrid plugging is always on here.
    Nova's _nova_to_osvif_vif_ovs() builds a single port profile, copies
    create_tap onto it from vif_details, and only then branches between
    VIFBridge (hybrid) and VIFOpenVSwitch, so the VIFBridge inherits a
    flag it cannot honour. os-vif then rejects the plug outright with
    "Tap device creation requested for unsupported VIF type. create_tap
    is only supported for VIFOpenVSwitch, got VIFBridge", nova reschedules
    until it runs out of hosts, and the instance lands in ERROR. No guest
    boots at all.
    
    The nova and os-vif halves of this have been in place since early
    2026 and were simply dormant; the Neutron flag is what arms them.
    Opt out in the ML2 config for openvswitch deployments until the
    upstream ordering is fixed. The flag is marked deprecated-for-removal
    from birth (deprecated_since 2026.2, LP#2069718) and exists only for
    this transition, so this override is expected to be short lived.
    Deployments using ML2/OVN are untouched.
    
    Prompt: Michael asked me to unblock CI by landing a patch that turns
    off ovs_create_tap, after we traced the kerbside OpenStack lane going
    red on 2026-08-03 to this three-way interaction and confirmed via the
    CI artifact bundles that nova was byte-identical across the last
    passing and first failing runs while neutron moved dev79 to dev88.
    
